```

## Purpose

Continue lifecycle modularization conservatively by moving native-boundary/runtime-unhealthy helper behavior into an explicit parent-side coordinator module.

The goal is to reduce lifecycle/native-boundary complexity in `inference.mjs` while preserving behavior and preparing safer future extraction of session reset, shutdown, model reset, and init coordinators.

This branch complements the existing pure policy module:

```text
nativeOperationPolicy.mjs
```

`nativeOperationPolicy.mjs` remains responsible for native hard-stop config validation/resolution and native operation timeout error construction.

The new coordinator owns only parent-runtime native-boundary helper behavior that depends on explicit lifecycle state or a caller-provided native hard-stop policy config.

## Implementation summary

Added:

```text
nativeBoundaryCoordinator.mjs
```

The new module exports:

```js
export function createRuntimeUnhealthyError(lifecycle) { ... }
export function assertRuntimeHealthy(lifecycle) { ... }
export function markRuntimeUnhealthy(lifecycle, { operation, sessionId = null, timeoutMs }) { ... }
export async function waitForNativeOperationBoundary(promise, timeoutMs, label, hardStopConfig) { ... }
```

`nativeBoundaryCoordinator.mjs` imports only:

```js
import { createNativeOperationTimeoutError } from "./nativeOperationPolicy.mjs";
```

`inference.mjs` now imports:

```js
import { resolveNativeOperationHardStopConfig } from "./nativeOperationPolicy.mjs";
import {
    assertRuntimeHealthy,
    markRuntimeUnhealthy,
    waitForNativeOperationBoundary
} from "./nativeBoundaryCoordinator.mjs";
```

Former local calls were mechanically rewired to pass the explicit lifecycle state object:

```text
assertRuntimeHealthy() -> assertRuntimeHealthy(lifecycle)
markRuntimeUnhealthy({...}) -> markRuntimeUnhealthy(lifecycle, {...})
```

`waitForNativeOperationBoundary()` kept the current explicit callsite shape:

```text
waitForNativeOperationBoundary(boundaryPromise, timeoutMs, label, hardStopConfig)
```

All current callsites already pass `hardStopConfig` explicitly. The helper does not hide config resolution and does not import the base config singleton.

## What intentionally stayed in `inference.mjs`

The following behavior-bearing code remains in `inference.mjs`:

```text
initModel()
ensureModelReady()
runInitCycle()
attemptInitOnce()
createInitPlan()
createFixedInitPlanFromLastSuccess()
worker message routing
resetSession()
resetModel()
finalizeWorkerShutdown()
shutdownRuntime()
shutdownAbort()
shutdownDrain()
shutdownDrainWithTimeout()
waiter creation/cleanup
scheduler creation/ownership
request cancellation/settlement loops
worker terminate/recreate flow
request settlement dependency wiring
public API exports
```

Reason:

- this branch is a native-boundary helper seam only;
- reset/session/shutdown/init coordinator extraction remains higher-risk and should be handled in later narrow branches;
- scheduler, workerBridge, request settlement, and worker-local execution remain separate architecture boundaries and were not moved.

## Behavior preservation notes

No intentional changes to:

```text
public API shape
error text
prompt/output semantics
request settlement order
cancellation ordering
scheduler queue/in-flight ownership
worker lifecycle/replacement behavior
worker operation serialization
configOverride validation
retry/profile planning
hardware probing behavior
native operation hard-stop policy
shutdown mode semantics
model path/model identity policy
```

Important preserved native-boundary details:

```text
runtime unhealthy state is still stored on lifecycle.runtimeUnhealthy
first native timeout still wins and later markRuntimeUnhealthy() calls do not overwrite the stored details
createRuntimeUnhealthyError() still reconstructs an Error from lifecycle.runtimeUnhealthy
stored unhealthy details still include phase, operation, sessionId, timeoutMs, message, and at
returned unhealthy Error still copies phase, operation, sessionId, and timeoutMs, but not at
native timeout errors still come from createNativeOperationTimeoutError()
waitForNativeOperationBoundary() still does not mark runtime unhealthy by itself
waitForNativeOperationBoundary() still does not cancel, terminate, recreate, or send worker messages
waitForNativeOperationBoundary() still returns { timedOut: false } on success and { timedOut: true, label, timeoutMs } on timeout
original boundary rejection still propagates if it wins the race
```

Important preserved caller-owned timeout distinctions:

```text
resetSession() timeout does not mark global runtime unhealthy
resetSession() timeout leaves the session waiter timed out and the session blocked until completion/restart
resetModel() timeout marks global runtime unhealthy with operation "resetModel"
shutdown timeout marks global runtime unhealthy with operation "shutdown"
```

Important preserved validation-order detail:

```text
shutdownRuntime() still resolves native hard-stop config before assertRuntimeHealthy(lifecycle)
```

This is preserved by keeping hard-stop config resolution in `inference.mjs` callsites rather than hiding config resolution inside the coordinator.

## Test fixture propagation

Several smoke tests create temporary mock runtime trees using fixed `RUNTIME_FILES` lists. Because `inference.mjs` now imports `nativeBoundaryCoordinator.mjs`, those fixture lists were updated.

Updated fixture lists in:

```text
tests/smokeTestContextCreationCancelBoundary.mjs
tests/smokeTestContextCreationRetry.mjs
tests/smokeTestDrainShutdown.mjs
tests/smokeTestInitThenResetWithoutPriorPrompt.mjs
tests/smokeTestNativeOperationHardStopPolicy.mjs
tests/smokeTestWorkerNativeCancellationBoundary.mjs
tests/smokeTestWorkerOperationSerialization.mjs
```

Each fixture list now includes the current modularization helper set needed by `inference.mjs`:

```text
nativeOperationPolicy.mjs
nativeBoundaryCoordinator.mjs
runtimeRequestSettlement.mjs
runtimeLifecycleState.mjs
```

No test assertions were intentionally changed.

